error[ffi_unknown_tag]: `fixedbugs-145-types.h` has no `struct anon_s` — clang read the header, and the struct it cannot lay out is an empty one C made up at this line
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-145-a-typedef-with-nothing-else-said-of-it.hero:18:18
     |
  18 |     record S tag anon_s  #~ ffi_unknown_tag
     |                  ^^^^^^
  note: so the tag is MISSPELLED, and correcting it is the repair; or `anon_s` is not a tag at all but the name of a typedef, `typedef struct { … } anon_s;`, and a record takes a typedef by its own name, with no `tag`: `record anon_s` (§ 13)
